### Goal
Make it feel **alive**:
- When new data arrives and a skill has just unlocked (or the learner levelled up), **Spark celebrates, exactly once**. It never celebrates on page load, never repeats, and queues if two things happen at once.
- Connect to the backend's **WebSocket**, so updates arrive **instantly** instead of within 5 seconds, with polling as the safety net.

### How the WebSocket is used (read this first)
The backend's `/ws` doesn't send full progress. It sends small events (`level_up`, `badge_unlocked`), and nothing at all for plain XP gains. So we treat the socket as a **doorbell**:
- **Any message** → fetch fresh progress **right now**. This works by changing the polling hook's `refreshKey`.
- **While the socket is open**, polling slows to every **30 seconds** instead of stopping, so XP gains the socket doesn't announce still arrive.
- **If the socket is closed**, or there is no `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL` (mock mode), polling runs at the normal speed.

The pages and visuals don't change at all. They just call `useLiveProgress()` instead of `useProgressPolling()`.

